{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530772-v20-augustus-embrace","id":1530772,"title":"V20 Augustus Embrace","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-13T18:26:42-08:00","id":1530772,"title":"V20 Augustus Embrace","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have doubts about the timeline and status of the Giovanni right after Augustus was embraced.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Did Augustus became a Cappadocian, or immediately created the bloodline Giovanni?</li> <li>IF he was a Cappadocian until the diablere of Cappadocius, was the act of diablere what transformed him into a Giovanni (Clan)?</li> <li>Is it known whether Augustus has either the Cappadocian, the Giovanni, or both clan weaknesses?</li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T20:56:06-08:00","id":1530778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530772-v20-augustus-embrace#post1530772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have doubts about the timeline and status of the Giovanni right after Augustus was embraced.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Did Augustus became a Cappadocian, or immediately created the bloodline Giovanni?</li> <li>IF he was a Cappadocian until the diablere of Cappadocius, was the act of diablere what transformed him into a Giovanni (Clan)?</li> <li>Is it known whether Augustus has either the Cappadocian, the Giovanni, or both clan weaknesses?</li> </ol>Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>1-2: Necromancy was developed by the Giovanni pretty much from the get-go or almost - the knowledge of its first 3 levels was basically common knowledge amongst those descended from Augustus line even in 1197, if Clanbook: Cappadocian serves as any indicator.<br /> <br /> 2-3: The Giovanni weakness supposedly originates in a curse from <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lamia_(Founder)\" target=\"_blank\">Lamia</a> before her destruction, what is kind of bizarre, considering she was 5th gen while Augustus started as 4th and had already consumed Cappadocius by that time. But then there's the whole &quot;priestess of Lilith&quot; thing and why the heck would Augustus think of diablerizing her as some claim he did, in the first place... (same goes for the Giovanni favoring Potence like the Lamia)<br /> <br /> I know it ain't much, but hope that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-14-2024, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T21:24:09-08:00","id":1530780,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's a concrete answer written anywhere so I can only offer how I interpret things, you'll have to decide what he was for your personal canon. The following is my nerd rant <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> DAV20 takes place in 1242 (2 centuries since Augustus' embrace) and offers the Giovan(n)i as their own separate entry in the Bloodline section who still share the Cappadocian clan disciplines, and the younger Giovanni retain the deathly pallor as a weakness. But it states that Auggie and his closest descendants never lost the ability to use the Blush of Life yet already had a painful bite, even though they shouldn't be afflicted with the Curse of Lamia for another couple centuries, which is hypothesized in-lore to be because &quot;the horrors he saw as a mortal man carried through his blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> I assume everyone who had the painful bite by 1242 were the only ones who knew of and were directly involved in the conspiracy to usurp the Cappadocians, and subconsciously the Blood was instantly distancing itself from the parent clan as if it had a mind of its own<br /> <br /> Vitae is quite spiritual and doesn't always have codified rules for what it can and can't do when its so potent, so maybe their refusal to consider themselves Cappadocians for eternity put the foot in the door for the bloodline to begin. The younger Giovanni who didn't know of the plot might not have considered themselves Cappadocians either but they didn't have the ability nor intention to overtake the parent clan, so maybe their Beast's were resigned to being ashy skeletons forever. Meanwhile the eldest Giovanni had entered unlife knowing the clan they were brought into was just a stepping stone and not their final form, already preparing to shed the skin they were forced to wear so long as Cappadocius was the Antediluvian<br /> <br /> The diablerie of Cappadocius definitely cemented the Giovanni as a clan wholly removed from the Cappies, but I think it would have happened anyway after a few hundred more years if the Conspiracy of Isaac never succeeded, with the caveat being the vast majority of the bloodline wouldn't have the painful bite and kept the deathly pallor. The Gio clanbooks explain that Potence and Dominate naturally suit the macho demeanor of a proud Italian man, so those might very well have become the bloodline's Disciplines naturally kinda like how the City Gangrel slowly shifted theirs yet kept the Gangrel weakness<br /> <br /> Its worth noting that Augustus' childe Cladius (the main instigator of Cappadocius' death) didn't have a single dot of Auspex or Fortitude even after 400 years when the diablerie happened, so I think he was an entirely different clan from the first night he was embraced, along with most of the other main conspiracists. At the same time its pretty trivial to pickup out of clan Disciplines at such a low generation so I can't actually point to that as hard evidence, that's just how justify that part of Cladius' loresheet. Still, you'd think an Elder would pick up at least one or two dots of Fortitude by accident if they were naturally inclined towards it<br /> <br /> <u><b>tldr</b></u>: 1. Augustus and his main goons were always a separate bloodline, 2. the diablerie itself might have swapped the clan's disciplines to what the eldest Giovanni preferred and the Lamia curse finished the job by giving the future generations of the clan Augustus' gnarly bite, and 3. he never had the Cappadocian curse<br /> <br /> This is all based on how V20 posits things so I can't offer any insight as to how the previous versions reconciled the Gio/Capp divide, its basically just me filling in the lore's blanks with speculative headcanon. Man do I love Cappadocian lore tho\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","name":"abugintherug","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28284_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T22:14:00-08:00","id":1530781,"title":"","content":"I assumed Augustus was a Cappadocian but became his own clan when he diablerized Cappadocius.<br /> <br /> And that any Giovanni Embraced before the clan diablerie are still Cappadocians.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T08:05:55-08:00","id":1530818,"title":"","content":"One could also suggest that one of the main reason behind the introduction of the Lamia bloodline and their doomed fate back in the original Dark Ages Companion was to help in setting up a sort of in-setting explanation/patch up for the Giovanni's divergence in discipline set and weakness from the Cappadocians as introduced in VtDA, but that's probably a little too cynical &amp; meta (and has some issues of its own, as pointed out in my previous post), so let's not do that and leave such sundry details alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530772-v20-augustus-embrace?p=1530781#post1530781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed Augustus was a Cappadocian but became his own clan when he diablerized Cappadocius.<br /> <br /> And that any Giovanni Embraced before the clan diablerie are still Cappadocians.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's convoluted - as the previous posts can sort of demonstrate with tidbits remembered from past books, the VtDA/DAV series have always tinkered with the (dis)continuity of things between Cappadocian and Giovanni, with the change showing signs here and there much before Cappadocius' fall.<br /> <br /> I think i even remember something about &quot;<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Premascine\" target=\"_blank\">Premascine</a>&quot; sometimes being used not just as a term for any Giovanni embraced before Augustus' rise to the top, but also disparaginly for any member of the clan that for mysterious reasons would manifest the Cappadocian weakness or others atavistic qualities (merits &amp; flaws) associated with the previous Clan of Death. So, one might say it could go sort of weirdly full circle i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-14-2024, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T13:13:35-08:00","id":1530841,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=lbeaumanior;n1530772]Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have doubts about the timeline and status of the Giovanni right after Augustus was embraced.[LIST=1][*]Did Augustus became a Cappadocian, or immediately created the bloodline Giovanni?<br /> <br /> Augustus was a Cappadocian after his embrace and would have the traditional clan weakness of a deathly palor and indeed there are Giovanni elders who share that trait.[*]IF he was a Cappadocian until the diablere of Cappadocius, was the act of diablere what transformed him into a Giovanni (Clan)?<br /> <br /> I think I would go with Lamia using the power of Lilith to curse him after he took her vitae and that it altered his weakness to painful bite.[*]Is it known whether Augustus has either the Cappadocian, the Giovanni, or both clan weaknesses?<br /> <br /> I'd go with with that the Giovannu faction during the Dark Ages had the original clan weakness.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T20:46:12-08:00","id":1530863,"title":"","content":"According to VDA20, Augustus Giovani and his closest clanmates had a painful bite, while other Giovani had the Cappadocian weakness. I presume these other Giovani with the Cappadocian weakness were embraced by Cappadocians, not by Augustus or his childer, and were Giovani by mortal family and affiliation, rather than by embrace, as part of the broader plan to bring the family into the clan.<br /> <br /> Also, the painful bite is not the same as the Lamia weakness (infectious bite), even though it would be later called Lamia's curse. And the painful bite becomes the weakness of all Hecata in V5.<br /> <br /> I don't know if the authors had a clear metaplot idea on this issue. An answer may be given in V5 Hecata material, since Nagaraja, Harbingers of the Skull, Giovanni, etc. now all have the same weakness (the painful bite), but we still don't know why.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that Cappadocius was an entropic mage before the Embrace, given that he and his descendants all have the signs of jhor. I can't think of a reason why Lamia and Giovani would have two different bite-related curses, nor why all Hecata would take this curse later on, but there's clearly some good reason implied.<br /> <br /> Augustus Giovani was a death mage before the Embrace. Perhaps he avoided the normal Cappadoci curse in part (he still looks like a corpse, but he can hide it with blood) because he could take precautions against jhor before the Embrace. He shows, however, a psychological sign of jhor: obsession with tearing down the Shroud.<br /> <br /> A very weak theory, more poetical than probable, could be that Lamia got her curse because Lilith is the Mother of Monsters, but the curse of Caine (and Lilith's possible dislike for the children of Adam, though she doesn't seem bitter in Revelations of the Dark Mother over that, and doesn't have much reason to be) twisted that into infecting humans somehow. Lamia was not interested in death particularly, neither before nor after the Embrace, so her bloodline have no sign of jhor.<br /> Augustus was embraced within Cappadocius larger plan to diablerise God and was already on his own a callous devourer of wealth and souls as the head of the Giovani necromerchants. He might have avoided for himself some marks of jhor (he was quite mundane and attached to life and power for Cappadocian standards after all), but his greed and disregard for the pain he inflicted manifested in his own curse.<br /> <br /> Nagaraja, Lamia and Giovanni all destroy or infect or hurt what they feed on. If Cappadocii and Samedi (and jhor tainted mages in general) obsess over death and take on its visage, Nagaraja, Lamia and Giovanni manifest Oblivion's destructive Maw who seeks to destroy all life.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T11:50:07-07:00","id":1536105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530772-v20-augustus-embrace?p=1530863#post1530863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to VDA20, Augustus Giovani and his closest clanmates had a painful bite, while other Giovani had the Cappadocian weakness. I presume these other Giovani with the Cappadocian weakness were embraced by Cappadocians, not by Augustus or his childer, and were Giovani by mortal family and affiliation, rather than by embrace, as part of the broader plan to bring the family into the clan.<br /> <br /> Also, the painful bite is not the same as the Lamia weakness (infectious bite), even though it would be later called Lamia's curse. And the painful bite becomes the weakness of all Hecata in V5.<br /> <br /> I don't know if the authors had a clear metaplot idea on this issue. An answer may be given in V5 Hecata material, since Nagaraja, Harbingers of the Skull, Giovanni, etc. now all have the same weakness (the painful bite), but we still don't know why.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that Cappadocius was an entropic mage before the Embrace, given that he and his descendants all have the signs of jhor. I can't think of a reason why Lamia and Giovani would have two different bite-related curses, nor why all Hecata would take this curse later on, but there's clearly some good reason implied.<br /> <br /> Augustus Giovani was a death mage before the Embrace. Perhaps he avoided the normal Cappadoci curse in part (he still looks like a corpse, but he can hide it with blood) because he could take precautions against jhor before the Embrace. He shows, however, a psychological sign of jhor: obsession with tearing down the Shroud.<br /> <br /> A very weak theory, more poetical than probable, could be that Lamia got her curse because Lilith is the Mother of Monsters, but the curse of Caine (and Lilith's possible dislike for the children of Adam, though she doesn't seem bitter in Revelations of the Dark Mother over that, and doesn't have much reason to be) twisted that into infecting humans somehow. Lamia was not interested in death particularly, neither before nor after the Embrace, so her bloodline have no sign of jhor.<br /> Augustus was embraced within Cappadocius larger plan to diablerise God and was already on his own a callous devourer of wealth and souls as the head of the Giovani necromerchants. He might have avoided for himself some marks of jhor (he was quite mundane and attached to life and power for Cappadocian standards after all), but his greed and disregard for the pain he inflicted manifested in his own curse.<br /> <br /> Nagaraja, Lamia and Giovanni all destroy or infect or hurt what they feed on. If Cappadocii and Samedi (and jhor tainted mages in general) obsess over death and take on its visage, Nagaraja, Lamia and Giovanni manifest Oblivion's destructive Maw who seeks to destroy all life.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm partial to Occam's Razor, so for me there were idiosyncrasies because that's not unheard of to happen, but Lamia's Curse cemented everything.<br /> <br /> But whatever the case, you just defined my headcanon that Cappadocius was an Awakened in Jhor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T05:45:45-07:00","id":1536500,"title":"","content":"I submit to the gallery that Augustus Giovanni was not embraced, and is not a vampire.<br /> <br /> All information that we have about Augustus is very clear that he was drained of blood by Constancia and Japheth using primitive medical tools, then Cappadocius gave them a quantity of vitae in a clay pot which was used on Augustus. They only used <b>some </b>of the vitae, the rest being sealed with wax and being ensorceled, which became known as the <b>True Vessel</b>. Augustus is only said to have had one childe, which is Claudius whom was his biological child, and there is no proof except of rumor that he actually embraced Claudius. Claudius was &quot;killed&quot; by Augustus when, Claudius sacked the Erinyes Temple and potentially destroyed the True Vessel. His body was given to Lazarus/Capuchin for some reason.<br /> <br /> Do note that one of the scenarios that happen in Giovanni Chronicles I has it, during the &quot;diablerie&quot; of Cappadocious there's and aside if the players were to some how kill Augustus; Cappadocious will bring him back to [un]life some how so that Augustus can finish the &quot;diablerie&quot;. I say &quot;diablerie&quot; in quotes because Augustus only gets Cappadocious' blood and not his soul, which is the requirement for a diablerie, as Cappadocious' soul flees beyond the Shroud. Before the Giovanni were introduced into the clan, the Cappadocians were masters of the physical body, disease, and its death. Logically antedeluvian level Mortis should be something like &quot;Create Revenant,&quot; or an equivalent undead creature.<br /> <br /> Therefore, Augustus is a Psuedo Vampire Zombu type creature, that was created to be the repository of Cappadocious' earthly power so that he could explore the Underworld and attempt to diablerize God which he believed was accessible from there. After he would use Augustus to re-inhabit the physical realm with his new power, but well the Maelstrom really did a number on him, and he became a Spectre.<br /> <br /> As for the other Giovanni, they're just Cappadocian offshoots like the Lamia, and gained their own version of a similar &quot;curse.&quot; The painful bite has several supposed origins: Curse from Lamia, As a result of the True Vessel Curse by Japheth, or a botched embrace. There are supposed records of Giovanni Cappadocians with the painful bite long before the Conspiracy of Issac, so the whole Lamia curse thing is mostly apocryphal.<br /> <br /> In my opinion the Samedi are the same experiment that Cappadocius tried with Augustus, but it was done by Lazarus instead on The Baron. The difference between a 3rd generation and a 4th generation, trying the same thing would be why the Samedi had such an extreme version of the Cappadocian flaw. Lazarus was the one who embraced Lamia herself, and was for some reason deathly (heh) afraid of her because of something she told him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T12:09:13-07:00","id":1536518,"title":"","content":"I would love to know what Lamia said to her sire that made him so scared? But alas outside of fan speculation we will probably never really know why Lazarus got scared at that point of his existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-29-2024, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T22:41:19-07:00","id":1536551,"title":"","content":"Lazarus was embraced sometime between 0 CE and 100 CE, which lines up with the rumors he might be the Biblical Lazarus. Augustus was &quot;embraced&quot; around 1000 CE, and &quot;diablerized&quot; Cappadocious in 1444. Lazarus would have embraced Lamia sometime between those two points, most likely before Augustus' creation.<br /> <br /> If we take it as fact that Lazarus is the biblical Lazarus, and that Lamia really was some elder special Lilian with a line to Lilith, I would infer that she told him about the Gnostic relationship between Lilith and Jehova has depicted in the <sub>Erinyes Fragments</sub> (Edit: Woops I meant Chronicles of the Dark Mother.) That Lazarus' God, and his &quot;rebirth&quot; as the Christ etc, are or something else than what they seem.<br /> <br /> Interestingly the Erinyes Temple, was originally a Salubri holding, till the Cappadocians invaded and took it for themselves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","user":"Aydoo","date":". 05-31-2024, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T00:44:00-07:00","id":1536553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530772-v20-augustus-embrace?p=1536518#post1536518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to know what Lamia said to her sire that made him so scared? But alas outside of fan speculation we will probably never really know why Lazarus got scared at that point of his existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>A theory the books present is that it was a prophecy of the fate of Cappadocius and his Clan, which lead to Lazarus going to Egypt and (presumably) find the Spell of Life and ignore the call to Kaymakli. However, that alone doesn't explain why he would be so afraid of Lamia.<br /> <br /> A hint might be the first level of Deimos (or the subsequent Path versions) in which a Lamia can scare someone with a secret name of Lilith. My personal theory is that Lamia called Lazarus by his True Name, which would give her magical command over him. It also made Lazarus realize that her Embrace was a setup. That would at least explain why he tried to stay as far away from her as possible when her powers of divination would have been very useful to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 05-30-2024, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T11:06:19-07:00","id":1536573,"title":"","content":"That could work as a good solution Viodshaper of why he went to Egypt and stayed away from Lamia as he learned some truths that changed what he believed in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T12:16:33-07:00","id":1536679,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm a big fan of the notion that Augustus got consumed by the various necromantic lineages in the Last Supper to create a new clan/cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T12:07:20-07:00","id":1536708,"title":"","content":"Tis something I've always found interesting (but close to &quot;it seems like just a weird thing to create fake mystery&quot;) the whole True Vessel thing, the suspicions that Constancia and Japheth had about Augustus Embrace... <br /> <br /> For me, Augustus was Embraced Cappadocian, they never spoke of &quot;that's so weird, he isn't suffering our Curse!&quot; or anything that would assume he showed different traits. But, I can believe all those that descended him by Blood or by womb would suffer from any Curse laid upon him that would trickle down the family tree. So Lamia Curses could've either made him had the nasty bite (on top of the clan curse) or cemented it as something the entire Lineage would have.<br /> <br /> It is interesting how Augustus is Clan Cappadocian in the Last Supper, but Claudius is just Giovanni. <br /> I would say that the entire Giovanni line would have some strange quirks and mutations (like the Tremere and Caitiffs have), since they were already a long lineage of necromancers, full of weird magics working with them (the whole Jhor thing is really spot-on). Then you throw the Clan of Death, that is full of weird vicissitudes around them, with their dozens of split bloodlines, plus Cappadocius penchant for destiny. Than there is that ordeal of Japheth and Constancia keeping part of the founder's blood and soul in the True Vessel, like a canopic jar of a mummy, which I vaguely recall that they took some of Augustus blood in a different vessel too, but might be misremembering. <br /> Oh, and let's not forget how Augustus didn't become fully 3rd Generation, so he doesn't have the blood mandate (having the Founder power of decreeing to their entire Clan/Bloodline, like creating curses, beckoning all descendants, etc.).<br /> <br /> Which might make a big change in the Premascine Giovanni from the post ones, since the &quot;true Giovanni&quot; (as they are stated as a Clan modernly) would just come about after Augustus ascension. <br /> I also wonder if, beside Promise of 1528's loopholes, their whole subsidiary families/bloodlines is something to kind of finding substitutes for their faulty blood. And they are trying to build a frankenstein clan out of the best parts of the different bloodlines they are cultivating. Like a rich bastard sending professional goons the world-round to find him compatible donors for his dying ailing body.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Giovannis are a strange bunch, full of weird quirks. It's interesting to debate, although a true concrete answer that validates all the lore that has been developed I believe is not so viable, we'll have to pick and choose some parts. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T13:50:47-07:00","id":1536714,"title":"","content":"My take is that with all setbacks that various lineages suffered and the younger members of the Giovanni getting frustrated with being caught up in feuds that they didn\u2019t ask for started to open up lines of communication with the others groups and found common ground and gleaned that they stood a better chance of survival if they overthrew there elders and to cement the deal was to get Augustus and consume him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T03:37:14-07:00","id":1536734,"title":"","content":"Something just occurred to me...<br /> \u0130f memory serves me well, only 3rd gens and lower have been shown to be able to lay massive curses, unless they're using Daimoinon or Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> How did Lamia manage to curse the whole of the Giovanni clan?<br /> <br /> The curse may be false. Or Lamia might have reached 3rd gen somehow before Augustus. Maybe she diablerised Cappadocius successfully (better if after a 4th gen vampire) and then pretended to die. Maybe she secretly pulls the strings of the Clan of Death while her line is presumed extinct (which would be easier to make believe as a 3rd gen with the powers she could access).<br /> <br /> Maybe tearing the Shroud is a part of Lilith's plans, one she set in motion centuries ago, when her high priestess managed to infiltrate the Clan of Death.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T06:49:19-07:00","id":1536742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530772-v20-augustus-embrace?p=1536734#post1536734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something just occurred to me...<br /> \u0130f memory serves me well, only 3rd gens and lower have been shown to be able to lay massive curses, unless they're using Daimoinon or Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> How did Lamia manage to curse the whole of the Giovanni clan?<br /> <br /> The curse may be false. Or Lamia might have reached 3rd gen somehow before Augustus. Maybe she diablerised Cappadocius successfully (better if after a 4th gen vampire) and then pretended to die. Maybe she secretly pulls the strings of the Clan of Death while her line is presumed extinct (which would be easier to make believe as a 3rd gen with the powers she could access).<br /> <br /> Maybe tearing the Shroud is a part of Lilith's plans, one she set in motion centuries ago, when her high priestess managed to infiltrate the Clan of Death.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I think in that case the alternative explanation the books give that the painful bite is a result of Japheth putting a curse on Cappadocius' vitae before Augustus' Embrace is a bit more plausible. I think Giovanni Chronicles had him with Thauma 9, combined with the highly unorthodox mode of Embrace it would give him the means to do so. You know what would be funny? If Cappadocius chose the indirect Embrace because he modified the vitae too before handing it over to Japheth, and Augustus received the double whammy of two people spitting into the soup before it got to his table.<br /> Combined with the divergence between painful bite and infectious bite, it would also lend more support to the idea that Lamia sold the Cappadocians out and her diablery is just a cover story.<br /> <br /> Lilith's interest in Necromancy by proxy of Lamia is a bit curious tbh. She isn't much associated with the dead but more with demonic creatures, and I don't see her having much common ground with the goals of the Giovanni. What I <i>could </i>see though would be an interest in the Neverborn as fellow outsiders of creation, and the Shadowlands are one step in the direction of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T16:38:33-07:00","id":1536766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530772-v20-augustus-embrace?p=1536734#post1536734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something just occurred to me...<br /> \u0130f memory serves me well, only 3rd gens and lower have been shown to be able to lay massive curses, unless they're using Daimoinon or Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> How did Lamia manage to curse the whole of the Giovanni clan?<br /> <br /> The curse may be false. Or Lamia might have reached 3rd gen somehow before Augustus. Maybe she diablerised Cappadocius successfully (better if after a 4th gen vampire) and then pretended to die. Maybe she secretly pulls the strings of the Clan of Death while her line is presumed extinct (which would be easier to make believe as a 3rd gen with the powers she could access).<br /> <br /> Maybe tearing the Shroud is a part of Lilith's plans, one she set in motion centuries ago, when her high priestess managed to infiltrate the Clan of Death.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not an actual rule, and even if it was, it's just for curses coming from vampiric power. Lamia was a priestess of Lilith too, which means she could have other means to curse, including maybe True Faith, Hedge Magic and even Daimonion, if not some residual power of possibly being an Awakened before the Embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T17:43:54-07:00","id":1536775,"title":"","content":"So many options and sources of power that Lamia could have drawn upon to punish Augustus and his brood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T13:15:19-07:00","id":1536808,"title":"","content":"This entire discussion is why I never liked the idea of &quot;sub clans&quot; or the different set of in-clan Disciplines between the Giovanni and Cappadocians. It's also why while I am not interested in V5, I do like how they combined all the various sub clans of the Cappadocians back together.<br /> <br /> To get around this debate and establish continuity, I established in my chronicles a long time ago that all the Cappadocians and their offshoots had the same Discipline set, and had the same clan weakness. It's just that certain lineages also had an additional weakness in the form of a mandatory Flaw (which any PCs would get build points for). All Giovanni also had Gripped of the Damned (which prior Giovanni embraces developed as well because the Curse affected all of Augustus's lineage). The Samedi had the Monstrous flaw. Lamia had whatever the diseased blood Flaw was called. In my mind, it's easier and quicker to explain how these additional Flaws came about than trying to resolve all the retcons and edition changes.<br /> <br /> There are semantic discussions and esoteric continuity debates I do find fun to have, but this isn't one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T17:36:05-07:00","id":1536823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530772-v20-augustus-embrace?p=1536742#post1536742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith's interest in Necromancy by proxy of Lamia is a bit curious tbh. She isn't much associated with the dead but more with demonic creatures, and I don't see her having much common ground with the goals of the Giovanni. What I <i>could </i>see though would be an interest in the Neverborn as fellow outsiders of creation, and the Shadowlands are one step in the direction of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that Lilith has no such interest, and Lamia's embrace was just a whim of Lazarus. She founded a bloodline of warriors after all, not of necromancy scholars.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T05:38:38-07:00","id":1536836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530772-v20-augustus-embrace?p=1536742#post1536742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith's interest in Necromancy by proxy of Lamia is a bit curious tbh. She isn't much associated with the dead but more with demonic creatures, and I don't see her having much common ground with the goals of the Giovanni. What I <i>could </i>see though would be an interest in the Neverborn as fellow outsiders of creation, and the Shadowlands are one step in the direction of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends<br /> According to rabbinic literature her demonic offspring were sired by an archangel named Samael<br /> Samael / Satan is the king of all demons, <b>the angel of death</b>, the husband of the demonic Lilith<br /> This is sometimes accompanied by a Muslim legend that after leaving Adam Lilith slept with Satan, thus creating the demonic Djinn. - witch actually fits nicely why in WoD the Shedim who returned from the exile trace their lineage to Lilith, and consider her their queen (&quot;<i>malkah ha-shedim</i>&quot; is one of Lilith's traditional titles in Jewish folklore)<br /> Sumero-Babylonian and Mesopotamian mytholigy depicted Lilith as storm demon associated with wind and was thought to be a bearer of disease, illness, and death.<br /> So Lilith have more than one conection to Death, if we see that point of view<br /> In WoD true, there is not much connection to death and the Lamia worshipping her was always strange, but the real life counterpart is more unserstandable, the Lamia worshiping that version, who was bearer of disease, illness, and death ad their bite and the &quot;seed of Lilith&quot; could be traced that aspect<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T07:07:28-07:00","id":1536838,"title":"","content":"Good point, although I'm wary of older translations of Sumerian sources, because many adopted the abrahamic bias in word choice that came from later sources like the Talmud. What is commonly translated as 'demon' from Sumerian or Akkadian culture is actually closer to what would be filed under Spirit in the WoD. Some did bring disease, some protected against it. Some did both at the same time. Lilu and Lilitu were a subclass of night spirits associated with Inanna/Ishtar that varied between incubi/succubi and other kinds of fertility-related things, including health and disease. It's complicated.<br /> All ancient Mesopotamian religions also made a clear distinction between these spirits and ghosts, btw.<br /> <br /> But since WoD lore around her mainly draws from abrahamic mythology your point stands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T07:46:24-07:00","id":1536839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530772-v20-augustus-embrace?p=1536823#post1536823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could be that Lilith has no such interest, and Lamia's embrace was just a whim of Lazarus. She founded a bloodline of warriors after all, not of necromancy scholars.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Always an option <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But the circumstances of her Embrace make me seriously doubt that. From a meta perspective, if my goal was to introduce a bloodline of Bahari warriors, I would look at the Gangrel - but perhaps the Ahrimanes already occupied that slot. I think the books describe them as warrior-scholars, and that is closer to how I see them, too.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the Cappadocians were specifically chosen by Lamia as a parent Clan for some in-game reason, but have nothing but speculation to back that up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T17:09:06-07:00","id":1536853,"title":"","content":"I'm sure that there was a in game reason for making the Lamia a Cappadocian line instead of Banu Haqim or Tzimsce for that matter as they fit in there with some ease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}